{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgSXg3XVhwbCbgMtxKCU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the three candidate files for round 2, slot 1 (an exploratory slot), and the candidate passes the self-check (`OK`). On the smoke fit its ELPD-LOO is −3918.6. The current best model sits at −3285.7, so this candidate will probably not displace it and could be pruned at the end of the experiment.\n\n**Model name:** `gist_typicality_subjective_switch_coin`\n\n**Hypothesis:** The brief asked for a normative account with one distortion.\n- **Normative part:** people remember a sequence only by three things: how widely the running heads-minus-tails tally swings, how many times the coin switches sides, and how many different three-flip chunks it contains. A sequence looks random to the extent that a random coin would often produce a sequence with those same three values.\n- **The one distortion:** each person imagines a random coin that switches sides at their own rate, usually more than half the time, and judges how typical a sequence is under that coin.\n- **The choice:** people pick the more typical sequence. They differ in how decisively they act on the difference, which is aimed at the critique's point that people differ in how consistently they agree with the majority. Each person also has a small left/right lean.\n\n**Implementation:** No mixing of cues. I count every sequence of length 2 to 8 in advance, so the model only needs two inputs per pair: the difference in how many sequences share each sequence's three values (on a log scale), and the difference in switch counts. It has three per-person parameters (switching rate, decisiveness, side lean), each drawn from a population distribution with 400 slots so it can predict new participants.\n\n**Caveats from the smoke check:**\n- **R-hat:** the check ran one chain, so convergence wasn't verified. Admission will test it on its full fit.\n- **ELPD reliability:** 4.9% of trials had a high Pareto k, over the 1% tolerance, so on the smoke fit its ELPD-LOO is marked unreliable. If the full fit shows the same, it can't be exported as the winner.\n- **Novelty:** not checked against the other models, but none of the live models uses this typicality measure.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3021,"cache_read_input_tokens":81481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3021,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14a33179-a212-40a6-9de1-2c7ea5b431d0","uuid":"69f9be85-1235-4ab3-a9f7-9a743f541016","timestamp":"2026-10-04T02:53:32.459Z","request_id":"req_011CfgSXffCipt35C7gef29p"}
